# MTMapInjector configuration — copy this file to `.env` and edit.
#
# `.env` is read by mt_paths.py (Python pipeline) and by build.bat /
# modp.bat (Windows pipeline) on every run. Process env vars override
# these. Lines starting with '#' are comments; values may be quoted.
#
# Requirements for a working setup:
#   - Motor Town installed (Steam)
#   - this repo cloned
#   - Python 3.10+, .NET 8 SDK
#
# Everything else — repak, UAssetGUI, the Oodle dll, the pak AES key, and
# a matching .usmap mappings file — ships inside the repo (tools/ +
# mappings/ + a built-in key). The game pak is extracted on demand by
# bootstrap_extract.py. A clean clone needs no manual config.

# OPTIONAL. .usmap mappings file. Defaults to the one bundled in the
# repo's mappings/ folder (matches the shipped game version). Only set
# this to override with a .usmap for a different Motor Town version.
# Generate with UnrealMappingsDumper / Dumper-7 if you need a new one.
# MTMI_MAPPINGS=D:/MT/MotorTown719.usmap

# OPTIONAL. UAssetGUI engine tag for --tojson/--fromjson. Defaults to
# the basename of MTMI_MAPPINGS without the .usmap extension.
# MTMI_MAPPINGS_TAG=MotorTown719

# OPTIONAL. Steam game folder — the path Steam opens when you right-click
# Motor Town -> Manage -> Browse local files. Must contain
# MotorTown/Content/Paks/MotorTown-Windows.pak. Auto-detected from
# common Steam install drives when left unset; only set this if your
# install is somewhere unusual.
# MT_GAME_DIR=D:/SteamLibrary/steamapps/common/Motor Town

# OPTIONAL. Override the pak AES decryption key. A correct default is
# built in (the Motor Town key is public), so you normally leave this
# unset. Only needed if a future game update rotates the key.
# MT_AES_KEY=0x...

# OPTIONAL. Full extraction. When =1, the clearance step unpacks the
# ENTIRE game pak (every asset, several GB) instead of just the bundles
# the pipeline needs. Use this if you add features that clone actors
# whose transitive references aren't in the default bundles — it
# guarantees every UAssetAPI read resolves locally. Cached by pak
# fingerprint, so the heavy unpack only happens once per game version.
# MTMI_FULL_EXTRACT=1

# OPTIONAL. Use an existing FModel export instead of extracting from the
# game pak. Point at the folder containing DataAsset/, Maps/, Objects/.
# Run `python bootstrap_extract.py --fmodel` to force this mode.
# MT_FMODEL_EXPORT=D:/FModel/Output/Exports/MotorTown/Content

# OPTIONAL. Pre-extracted MotorTown/Content tree to use directly,
# bypassing bootstrap_extract entirely. Defaults to the repo's
# vanilla_extract/MotorTown/Content.
# MTMI_GAME_CONTENT=D:/MT/Output/Exports/MotorTown/Content

# OPTIONAL. UE editor cooked-content folder. Only needed if you author
# meshes in-editor and re-run import_meshes.py to refresh them.
# MTMI_COOKED_CONTENT=C:/Users/you/Documents/Unreal Projects/.../Content

# OPTIONAL. Repo root override for ue.py (the editor-side exporter).
# Auto-resolves to the folder containing mt_paths.py when unset.
# MTMI_REPO_ROOT=D:/MTLiveMap

# OPTIONAL. World-placement offset added to every editor-exported
# mesh/actor by import_meshes.py. Your custom build is authored in one
# spot in the editor and shifted into a chosen region of Jeju — set these
# to move the whole build. Defaults match the current "new map" location.
# MTMI_OFFSET_X=-512003.0
# MTMI_OFFSET_Y=123148.0
# MTMI_OFFSET_Z=-22180.0
# MTMI_OFFSET_PITCH=0.0
# MTMI_OFFSET_ROLL=0.0
# MTMI_OFFSET_YAW=0.0

# Mod identity. Names the staging folder and the deployed pak
# (zzzz_<name>.pak). Rename the folder to match if you change it.
MTMI_MOD_NAME=MapChangeTest_P
